      "message": "FWIW, I also wanted to implement it the way you are suggested. But I ran into compilation issues since the generated c file itself depends on headers specified in the parent cc_library.\n\ne.g. The .cpp file generated from system/tools/aidl/aidl_language_y.yy depends on [libbase headers](https://cs.android.com/android/_/android/platform/system/tools/aidl/+/db9a0dd0349127c3d91b92788e2aa8a04beac272:aidl_language_y.yy;l\u003d22;drc\u003d207c98ab02c7477d12953e946585b8df2597db60;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0) and this dependency is mentioned in the static_libs of [aidl](https://cs.android.com/android/_/android/platform/system/tools/aidl/+/db9a0dd0349127c3d91b92788e2aa8a04beac272:Android.bp;l\u003d43;drc\u003d0b25ca2e5c0e92aab6e05f49873b7f5fc54e086b;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0). We could propagate the required header information to the internal cc_static_library for compiling the generated c file, but then the dependency becomes two-directional, albeit just in bp2build.\n\n\nAre there other alternatives to reduce the duplication?",
